{"name":"Sable Evening","hex":"#5d5e58","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sable","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small carnivorous mammal of the Old World that resembles a weasel, Martes zibellina, from cold regions in Eurasia and the North Pacific islands, valued for its dark brown fur.","Any other marten, especially Martes americana (syn. Mustela americana)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sable-coloured, black.","In blazon, of the colour black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sable"},{"term":"evening","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day between afternoon and night.","The time of the day between the approximate time of midwinter dusk and midnight (compare afternoon); the period after the end of regular office working hours."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of even"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evening"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sable","blocks":[{"text":"The sable is a species of marten, a small omnivorous mammal primarily inhabiting the forest environments of Russia, from the Ural Mountains throughout Siberia, and northern Mongolia. Its habitat also borders eastern Kazakhstan, China, North Korea, and Hokkaido, Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sobol_bur.jpg/330px-Sobol_bur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable"},{"title":"Evening","blocks":[{"text":"Evening is the period of a day that begins at the end of afternoon and overlaps with the beginning of night. It starts when the sun is close to the horizon and, according to most definitions, spans the period of night before bedtime or midnight. The exact times when evening begins and ends are subjective and depend on location and time of year. In some cases, evening is considered to begin during daylight; before sunset."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Evening_in_Parambikkulam%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg/330px-Evening_in_Parambikkulam%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evening"},{"title":"Sable (tincture)","blocks":[{"text":"In heraldry, sable is the tincture equivalent to black. It is one of the five dark tinctures called colours."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable_(tincture)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Sable_area.png/500px-Sable_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Sable_area.png/500px-Sable_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASable_area.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sables.png/330px-Sables.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sables.png/330px-Sables.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration from Brehm's Life of Animals","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASables.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Russian_sable.jpg/500px-Russian_sable.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Russian_sable.jpg/500px-Russian_sable.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Russian sable, as illustrated in The Trapper's Guide, 1867. The Russian variety yields the most valuable sable fur.[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARussian_sable.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Wiki-ezokuroten1.jpg/500px-Wiki-ezokuroten1.j